WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.270
Last time on...

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.270
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.400
We'd been practicing for
the Love Live regional prelims.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.860
One day, Yoshiko-<i>chan</i> found a stray dog.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.280
And then, the dog's owner showed up.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.450
G-Glad to be of help.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.660
But believing that
encountering the dog was her destiny,

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.080
Yoshiko-<i>chan</i> couldn't give up.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.950
I wondered if such things 
really don't exist...

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.580
Things like destiny... Invisible powers...

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.830
I think invisible powers exist.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.670
Not just in you, but inside everyone.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.430
Here we go.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.100
We've seen this place before, <i>zura</i>!

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.480
This is the promised land
where the last Ragnarök took place.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.690
The regional prelims that we couldn't pass...

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.730
It's payback time.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.110
Yep!

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.320
Fifty-seven?

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.580
Right. As of today,
we have 57 prospective students.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.000
"Shine!"
"Love Live! Tokai Regional Prelims"

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.000
Can't be... Are you saying we couldn't
even add ten more this past month?

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:08.710
There's less than a month until the time limit
given by Mari's dad, isn't there?

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:15.720
"Shine!"
"Love Live! Tokai Regional Prelims"

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.210
The night that the Love Live
regional prelims will be held...

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.720
If we don't have a hundred
prospective students by then,

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.430
there will be nothing we can do.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.640
In other words, the regional prelims are...

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.140
Yes. Our last chance.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.400
So this means that we have no choice
but to stake our future on it, huh?

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:51.170
<i>Let's throw our all at each other</i>
<i>and grab hold of the future!</i>

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:01.800
<i>The sky and this ocean are both on our side</i>

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.770
<i>Shining and saying, "Go, do your best!"</i>

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:12.480
<i>To let our voices reach far, far away</i>

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.400
<i>Shall we shout our dreams louder?</i>

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.150
<i>(Full of hope)</i>

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:23.490
<i>Today pulls tomorrow toward itself</i>

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:32.080
<i>It's really fun to grasp the magnet</i>
<i>in my heart and run right now!</i>

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.210
<i>(Let's always go together)</i>

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:37.010
<i>What shall we do about the future?!</i>

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:44.810
<i>Everyone laughs and cries</i>
<i>as</i> <i>they</i> <i>look for the shape of their dreams</i>

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:53.230
<i>Because I'm sure the</i> <i>future</i> <i>us</i>
<i>will have the answer</i>

00:02:53.230 --> 00:03:01.320
<i>Let's run with everything we have</i>
<i>and become the shining wind</i>

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.660
<i>We got dream</i>

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:10.500
One, two, three, four!
One, two, three, four! Now change!

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.330
"'#6 Aqours WAVE'"

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.460
Up! Up!

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:17.760
Oh, good! I'd like to see your arms
raised at the same angle.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.340
Hanamaru, bring them up a bit higher.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.450
That's good!

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.000
Don't forget this angle.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:23.800
<i>Zura</i>...

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.260
Well then, let's practice individually
after taking a break.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.100
--Chika-<i>chan</i>! I bought some ice cream earlier.
Would you like some?
--I'm so beat, <i>zura</i>.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.310
--Really?!
--Are you okay, Hanamaru-<i>chan</i>?
--For a change of pace.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.730
<i>Zura</i>...

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.190
Whoa! They list the groups
that are considered

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.280
the most likely to go to the nationals.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.410
--<i>Zura</i>?
--Wait, what? There's something like that?

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:47.700
"Here are the school idols
who are considered the most likely
to go to the nationals!!"

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.320
Since Love Live is popular, there seem to be

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.700
many people who try
to predict that kind of stuff.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.660
What groups are in the list?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:54.830
Let's see... There are, of course,
those who went to the nationals last year.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:55.670
And...

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.670
Ah...

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.830
Saint Snow. They passed the last regional
prelims as the top-ranked group,

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.720
and won eighth place in the final round.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.720
The older sister Sarah
is a third-year student this year.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.230
This is her last chance,
so she's in it to win it.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.640
I bet both of them are pretty fired up.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.060
Let's see who else...

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.730
Ah, Aqours!

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.560
--What?!
--Really?!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.820
--See?
--That's us, <i>zura</i>.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.110
Hey, what're they saying about us?

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.280
Although Aqours didn't
pass the last regional prelims,

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.450
their performance in the qualifiers this year

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:33.870
was so splendid that it was a fair match
for the groups that went to the nationals.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.390
We're looking forward to seeing their growth.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.340
Looking forward...

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.760
If I use my dark powers as a fallen angel,

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.180
this is but a trifle!

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.970
Right. It is but a trifle!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:55.310
I would expect nothing less
from one who made a contract with me,

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.980
my little demon Lili!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.730
How insolent! Never have I signed
a contract with the likes of you!

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.990
--What's going on?
--"Lili"?

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.530
They sure must've fallen far, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.660
--Yeah.
--No! It's not like that!

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.540
Welcome to Hell Zone.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.620
Hold it!

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.910
I'm glad you guys seem to be having fun!

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.830
Even you, Chika-<i>chan</i>?!

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.660
It says that for
the regional prelims this time around,

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.610
the groups who will proceed
to the nationals will be decided

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.690
by the votes at the prelim sites
and on the internet.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.760
That's good! It's better than
having to wait to hear the results.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.470
It's not that simple.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.770
Each school's students will be at the site
to root for their school idol group.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.300
Even though they'll hold 
internet voting, too,

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.440
schools with many students
will still be at an advantage.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.690
Then could it be that...

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.030
That's right. In terms of number of students,

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.200
Uranohoshi has the biggest disadvantage.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.540
"Dance Formation Idea Notebook"

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.510
That may be the only answer after all.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.240
I think so, too.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:19.020
That brings back memories. 
So you kept it, huh?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.520
Don't tell me... you want to do it?

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:27.190
Don't tell me... you don't wanna do it?

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.740
You do understand
the situation we're in, don't you?

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.830
We have no choice but to take a chance on it.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:38.330
--But...
--My feelings haven't changed.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.460
Mari...

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.880
This time, I agree with Mari-<i>san</i>.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.420
We do everything we can
to keep our school alive.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:50.130
I think that's my duty as president
of the student council, so...

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.890
Moreover, this is our last chance.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.660
But this isn't something we can do.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:06:59.940
It's something we cannot do.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.820
That's not really true.
We were so close that time, too. So close...

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.780
But we couldn't.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.950
Worse than that, you injured your leg, Mari.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.490
It was my fault that I injured myself.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:17.700
I wanted to catch up with you,
so I tried too hard.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.790
She's right. Moreover, 
there are nine of us now.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.160
It's not just us.

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.090
No... we shouldn't!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.220
We tried to reach what we couldn't reach...

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.510
...and because of that, someone got hurt.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.590
And now, we are going to
push that on Chika and the others?

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:38.430
This has to...!

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.000
Mari!

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.960
Oof...!

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:14.930
Don't speak so negatively
about what we did together.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.460
Those memories are very precious to me.

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.310
That's why I want to see this through.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.930
I want to complete the Aqours
that we dreamed of back then.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.060
"Dance Formation Idea Notebook"

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.690
Shiitake looked at me...

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:42.410
Yes, among the performing groups,
we have the least number of students.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.870
You certainly are at a disadvantage.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.510
You'll just have to give 
a knockout performance

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.340
to overcome your disadvantage
in terms of number of students.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.380
Yeah, I know. But a knockout performance...

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.180
Sis, you can take a bath now.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.970
I think it's something more
than simply being good.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:04.400
In fact, many Love Live performers
these days can sing and dance

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.190
in the same league as our <i>sempai</i> idols.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.900
But no one thinks that they're equals.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:14.740
The shine of the pioneers
who established the popularity of Love Live

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.950
from the beginning...

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:20.280
The light that can never be reached...

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:23.200
The light that can't be reached...

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.420
What makes us Aqours?

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:28.670
Yeah.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.460
What does it mean for 
us to walk our own path?

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.800
What is our shine?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.470
I've come to realize that
it's important to find the answers

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.010
after performing in Love Live...

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.850
And yet, I still can't put them into words.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.730
They haven't taken shape yet.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.020
So I want them to take shape.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.190
Take shape...

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:58.100
To hear something like that
from Chika-<i>san</i> now... It must be fate.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.660
I'll tell them about <i>that</i>, okay?

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.660
What? But that's...

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.200
What? What're you talking about?

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.590
There's this formation that
the three of us created in order to advance

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.590
to the Love Live final round two years ago.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.000
Formation?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.380
--Falling Angels?
--<i>Zura</i>?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.850
Ra... Ra... Ra...?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.930
--We're not playing <i>shiritori</i>.
--Ah...

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.430
I didn't know there was something like that!
That's amazing! Teach us how!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.480
But Mari hurt her leg while trying to do it.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.060
In addition, it'll be a lot of work
for the other members, too.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.940
What point is there
in taking such a big risk now?

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.640
Why not?

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.410
Kanan-<i>chan</i>! When are we gonna do it
if we don't do it now?!

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.490
We made a promise
at the beginning, didn't we?!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.410
Let's struggle as hard as we can!
Love Live is right in front of us!

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:49.120
Now is the time to struggle!
I want us to do everything we can!

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:54.500
But this formation requires a lot
from the person in the center.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:59.470
It was me that time...
but can you really do it, Chika?!

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.470
I'll be fine. I'll do it!

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.590
Chika...

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:09.740
Looks like it's decided. Let's hand
that notebook over, Kanan-<i>san</i>.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:14.000
In order to make a breakthrough as Aqours,

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.320
there's a wall that we
must overcome without fail.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.950
Now may be that time.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:25.280
But let me tell you one thing.
If I judge that it's dangerous,

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.790
I'll stop you, Chika, even if it means
we have to withdraw from Love Live, okay?

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.900
Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.220
Chika! Be quiet!

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.970
It's more difficult than I thought...

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.970
Chika!

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.280
Chika!

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:54.300
I'm sorry, Mito-<i>nee</i>! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:56.680
You brat!

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.480
What're you gonna do about the doors?!

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.500
Stop disturbing our guests, Mito.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:02.610
R-Right.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.620
Here we go... Aah!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.050
Are you worried?

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.770
I was afraid it'd turn out like this.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.560
I wanted the three of 
us to do that formation.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.600
Then why are you having
Chika and the others do it?

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.560
It's like we're forcing it on them.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:37.790
I trust that Chika-<i>chi</i> can do it.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.780
The Aqours this time will definitely succeed.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.460
You believe that, too, right, Kanan?

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.730
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.410
Here we go!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:57.380
Chika! Go for it!

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.710
Are you okay?!

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.540
I-I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:07.970
One more time!

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.720
Let's take a little break.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.560
You've been doing this
for five days. You'll get sick.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:16.940
No, I can still keep going.
I feel like I'm almost there.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.400
There are only two weeks
until the regional prelims.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.400
If you push too hard and get injured now...

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.450
Yeah, I know.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.490
But I want to try.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:31.390
You know, when I sang
for the first time here, I thought...

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.870
...I couldn't have done anything
without everyone's support.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:39.710
At the Love Live regional prelims...
and the last qualifiers, too...

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.460
I was able to do my best
because I was with you guys.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.460
"Dance Formation Idea Notebook"

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:46.890
Everyone at school as well as
the townspeople have helped us, too.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.220
So, I want to repay their 
support at least once.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:54.130
I'll be careful not to get injured,
so let me try a little bit longer.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.000
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.820
Ow, ow, ow...

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.740
Are you okay?!

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.530
I'm fine!

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:12.950
I do understand how she feels,
but I'm still worried.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:14.910
Yeah.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.080
Then why don't you two stop her?

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:21.750
I think she's more likely
to listen to you guys than to me.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.960
You don't want to?

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:28.510
As I said, I do understand how she feels.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:29.470
Yeah.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.630
Chika-<i>chan</i> was the normal monster.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.350
Monster?

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:38.190
The normal monster, Chika-<i>chi</i>.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.400
Everything about her is normal.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.400
She's always watching
the sparkling light from afar.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.650
The truth is, she's got
incredible power, and yet...

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:51.580
She says she's just normal
and is always on the sidelines.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:56.610
So she thinks that she wants
to make it work on her own.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.750
Not just watching, but with her own hands...

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:16.680
Chika.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.580
Kanan-<i>chan</i>...?

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.630
Oh? What's going on, Riko-<i>chan</i>?

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.960
Ah, Shima-<i>san</i>. Where's Chika-<i>chan</i>?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.590
She said she'd go practice a little.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:54.420
Practice...? This late?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.980
Ouch!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.440
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.360
One more time.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:10.150
She said that if she asked you to come,
you'd probably stop her, so...

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.700
I'm sorry.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:15.950
That's okay. But it's in 
the middle of the night...

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:17.700
Well, after Kanan-<i>chan</i> said that to her...

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.910
Chika, promise me...

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.250
...that you'll give up if you can't
do it by tomorrow morning.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:29.400
You've worked hard, Chika.
But you must be at your limits.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.470
Kanan-<i>chan</i>...

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:37.890
Since she herself
was challenging it two years ago,

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:41.550
she may know better than anyone
how hard it is.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.540
She's so close.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.900
Yeah, very close.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.730
--Almost!
--Almost!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.030
Ahh, come on!

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.960
What am I doing wrong?

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.010
--Chika-<i>chan</i>!
--Chika-<i>chan</i>!

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:22.930
Don't get frustrated.
Relax and just practice like usual.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.520
Riko-<i>chan</i>...

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:25.940
You can do it.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.580
I know you can do it!

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.610
Hang in there!

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:33.610
We'll be watching you!

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:34.920
Okay!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.040
--Chika!
--Chika-<i>chan</i>!

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.580
Fight!

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.010
Go for it, <i>zura</i>!

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:02.150
Argh! This is supposed to be
the scene where I do it!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:07.730
Why...? Why can't I do it?

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:14.050
Riko-<i>chan</i>... You-<i>chan</i>...
Everyone's rooting for me so much, and yet...

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.200
No... I don't wanna give up!

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:23.800
I haven't done anything yet!
I haven't been able to do anything yet!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.580
Beep! Boom!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.380
Beeeeeeep!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:33.260
I'm the normal monster, You-<i>solo</i>!

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:36.720
Hey, I won't let you have your way!
Riko-<i>pi</i> is here, too!

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.680
--What?! Boooom!
--Bam!

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.350
Do you still think that 
you're a normal person?

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.330
What?

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.600
You're the normal monster Chika-<i>chi</i>.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:53.770
You're the leader, but you've come
this far because of everyone's help.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:57.570
But you haven't done anything at all.
You're thinking all that, aren't you?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.280
Yeah, because it's true.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:07.300
Chika-<i>chan</i>, who should you thank
for getting this far?

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:15.050
That's... everyone at school...
the townspeople, You-<i>chan</i>, Riko-<i>chan</i>,

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.780
--and...
--Haven't you forgotten
the most important person?

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:20.840
What?

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.930
Who should we thank for bringing
the current Aqours together?

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.630
Who suggested starting it first?

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:29.770
That's...

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:33.940
Because of you, Chika-<i>chan</i>,
I started being a school idol.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.900
So did I, and the others, too.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.850
No one else could've created
the current Aqours.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.320
Because of you, we're here now.

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.810
Don't forget that.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:04.300
Someone who thinks she's average
continues to challenge herself

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.680
without giving up...

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:09.290
I think that's pretty amazing!

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:12.480
I think it requires quite a bit of courage.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:16.360
That's who you are, Chika-<i>chan</i>.
That's why we all want to try our best.

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:19.610
That's why we wanted to be part of Aqours.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.450
Don't do this because you think
you owe it to all of us.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.460
We are all excited...

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:32.500
...about being able to find our own shine
together with you, Chika-<i>chan</i>.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.480
Everyone...

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.170
It's a new Aqours wave.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.470
Chika, it's time.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.300
Are you ready?

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:06.450
Thank you, Chika.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:31.810
<i>We'll push our limits until the end</i>

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:34.020
<i>(How'll it turn out? Heart-pounding wave)</i>

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.980
<i>It's time to overcome our impatient selves</i>

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.270
<i>(That's right! Wave!! Go beyond)</i>

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:42.190
<i>We can't think about anything else</i>

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:44.530
<i>(How'll it turn out? Heart-pounding wave)</i>

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:47.530
<i>Our dreams that have become one, run on</i>

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.870
<i>(That's right! Wave!! Can't stop)</i>

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:54.790
<i>So frustrated, we can't sit still</i>

00:21:54.790 --> 00:22:03.050
<i>I'm sure everyone understands that feeling</i>

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:08.840
<i>Can we do it? (Hi!) We can! (Hi!)</i>

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:12.850
<i>My heart crying out</i>
<i>(and the shine it craves)</i>

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:16.140
<i>Will prove it right before your eyes</i>

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:19.270
<i>Can we do it? (Hi!) We can! (Hi!)</i>

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:26.570
<i>That's the only choice (we decided)</i>
<i>with super passionate jumps</i>

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:31.830
<i>Can we grab hold of a new light?</i>

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.790
<i>Let's believe (Yeah!)</i>

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:42.880
<i>A "miracle wave" brings miracles</i>

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:03.230
I am so happy that the nine of us
were able to sing here together today.

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:06.530
Our own way of shining...

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:10.950
What is it? What kind of form does it take?

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:18.210
What the nine of us saw...
What moved us... What we want to aim for...

00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:23.250
Our shine is in those
sincere feelings... I'm sure of it!

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:27.010
Thank you for believing in me, everyone!

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:33.880
Wooooo, yeah!

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:38.500
Next Time! "The Time Left."

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:41.410
"#7 'The Time Left'"
